The Chief of Police is authorized to exercise such powers as may be necessary or convenient to carry out and effectuate the purpose and provisions of this article and O.C.G.A. §§ 41-2-7—41-2-10 and 41-2-12—41-2-17, including the following powers in addition to others granted in O.C.G.A. §§ 41-2-7—41-2-10 and 41-2-12—41-2-17:
(1) To investigate the dwelling conditions in the unincorporated area of the City in order to determine which dwellings, buildings or structures therein are unfit for human habitation or for commercial, industrial or business use a or are vacant, dilapidated, and being used in connection with the commission of drug crimes;
(2) To administer oaths and affirmations, to examine witnesses and to receive evidence;
(3) To enter upon premises for the purpose of making examinations; however, such entries shall be made in such manner as to cause the least possible inconvenience to the persons in possession;
(4) To appoint and fix the duties of such officers, agents and employees as he or she deems necessary to carry out the purposes of the ordinances; and
(5) To delegate any of his or her functions and powers under the ordinance to such officers and agents as he or she may designate.
(Code 2005, § 10-65; Ord. of 1-11-2016)
State Law reference— Powers of public officers, O.C.G.A. § 41-2-11.

