(a) Public property—City parks. It shall be unlawful to reside or to store personal property in any park owned by the City. No person shall occupy public property for habitation. No person shall reside in a vehicle or structure on public property except as part of a City event.
(b) Public property—Sidewalks. It shall be unlawful to sleep, lie down, reside or to store personal property on any sidewalk in the City.
(c) Public property—Blocking ingress and egress. It shall be unlawful to use any public place to sleep, lie down, to reside or to store personal property or to sit or lie down on any public property so as to interfere with the ingress or egress from a building.
(d) Public property—Urban camping. It shall be unlawful to use any public place, including City parks and sidewalks, for living accommodations or camping.
(e) Urban camping on private property without the owner's permission. It shall be unlawful for anyone to camp, sleep, reside, store personal property, or lie down outside on any private property without the owner's or leaseholder's permission.
(f) Definitions. For purposes of this section, the term "storage" means leaving one's personal effects, such as, but not limited to, clothing, bedrolls, cookware, sleeping bags, luggage, knapsacks, or backpacks, unattended for more than one hour. City parks shall expressly include, but not be limited to, City greenways, trails, and other pedestrian paths and areas.
(g) Exceptions. Notwithstanding anything in this section to the contrary, this section shall not apply to nor be construed to prohibit the following behavior:
(1) Persons sitting or lying down as a result of a medical emergency;
(2) Persons sitting in wheelchairs while using parks, sidewalks, or other public places;
(3) Persons sitting down while attending parades for which valid permits have been issued;
(4) Persons sitting down while patronizing outdoor cafes;
(5) Persons sitting on chairs or benches supplied by a public agency or abutting private property owner;
(6) Persons sitting down, lying down or napping while attending performances, festivals and concerts taking place in any park, street or sidewalk closed by permit for such purpose;
(7) Persons sitting on seats in bus zones occupied by people waiting for the bus;
(8) Persons sitting or lying down while waiting in an orderly line outside a box office to purchase tickets to any sporting event, concert, performance, or other special event;
(9) Children under the age of 13 years sleeping in parks, or sleeping anywhere else while being carried by an accompanying person or while sitting or lying in a stroller or baby carriage; or
(10) Persons lying down or napping during park hours.
(h) Penalties. Any person who violates any provision of this section may be subject to arrest or summoned to appear in court and, upon conviction or other finding of guilt, may be punished by a fine of up to $1,000.00 or 60 days of imprisonment, or both.
(Code 2005, § 58-46; Ord. No. 1403, 1-13-2011)

